    {
      "number": 9,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 13,
      "stem": "The mass $R$ of a standard packet is normally distributed with mean 500 g and standard deviation 18 g. Packets are sampled independently. A premium variety has a normally distributed mass $C$, with lower quartile 724 g and interquartile range 52 g.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the probability that a standard packet has mass less than 480 g.",
          "marks": 1
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Given that a standard packet has mass greater than 480 g, find the probability that it has mass less than 500 g.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Find $a$ such that 15% of standard packets have mass greater than $a$ grams.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "d",
          "prompt": "Five standard packets are selected. Find the probability that exactly one has mass less than 480 g.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "e(i)",
          "prompt": "Find the mean of the premium mass distribution.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "e(ii)",
          "prompt": "Find the standard deviation of the premium mass distribution.",
          "marks": 3
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "0.133; conditional 0.423; cutoff 519 g; exactlyone 0.376; premium mean 750 g and SD 38.5 g.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P(R<480)=0.133260\\ldots\\approx0.133$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Use $P(480<R<500)/P(R>480)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$0.366739\\ldots/0.866739\\ldots=0.423126\\ldots\\approx0.423$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Find the 85 th percentile of $N(500,18^2)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$a=518.6558\\ldots\\approx519$g."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Let the count be $B\\sim\\operatorname{Bin}(5,p)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Use $p=0.133260\\ldots$ without premature rounding."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$P(B=1)=5p(1-p)^4=0.376032\\ldots\\approx0.376$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "By normal symmetry, $Q_3=724+52=776$ and the mean is midway between the quartiles."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\mu=(724+776)/2=750$g."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "e(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$P(C<724)=0.25$."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$z_{0.25}=(724-750)/\\sigma=-26/\\sigma=-0.674489\\ldots$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$\\sigma=38.54765\\ldots\\approx38.5$g."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourcePages": [
        10
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "section": "B",
      "marks": 13,
      "stem": "The curves $y=4\\cos x$ and $y=x^2$ intersect at $L$ and $R$, with $R$ having positive $x$-coordinate $r$. Angles are in radians. A rectangle has vertical sides at $x=-a$ and $x=a$, its upper vertices on $y=4\\cos x$ and lower vertices on $y=x^2$, where $0<a<r$. Its area is $A$.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": "a",
          "prompt": "Find the coordinates of $L$ and $R$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "b",
          "prompt": "Find the total area enclosed by the two curves.",
          "marks": 4
        },
        {
          "label": "c",
          "prompt": "Show that $A=8a\\cos a-2a^3$.",
          "marks": 2
        },
        {
          "label": "d(i)",
          "prompt": "Show that a stationary value of $A$ satisfies $\\dfrac{\\cos a-a\\sin a}{a^2}=\\dfrac34$.",
          "marks": 3
        },
        {
          "label": "d(ii)",
          "prompt": "Find the maximum possible area of the rectangle.",
          "marks": 2
        }
      ],
      "answerSummary": "Intersections $(\\pm1.20,1.44)$; enclosed area 6.30; rectangle area $8a\\cos a-2a^3$, maximum 3.60.",
      "markScheme": [
        {
          "part": "a",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$L=(-1.201538\\ldots,1.443694\\ldots)\\approx(-1.20,1.44)$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$R=(1.201538\\ldots,1.443694\\ldots)\\approx(1.20,1.44)$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "b",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Integrate upper minus lower between the intersection abscissae."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Use unrounded limits $-r,r$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The integral is $\\int_{-r}^{r}(4\\cos x-x^2)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "The enclosed area is $6.304327\\ldots\\approx6.30$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "c",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Base $=2a$ and height $=4\\cos a-a^2$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Their product is $8a\\cos a-2a^3$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d(i)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Differentiate using the product rule."
            },
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "$A\\,\\!\\prime(a)=8\\cos a-8a\\sin a-6a^2=0$."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "Because $a>0$, divide/rearrange to obtain $(\\cos a-a\\sin a)/a^2=3/4$."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "part": "d(ii)",
          "steps": [
            {
              "code": "M1",
              "text": "Maximize $A$ on $0<a<r$, by graphing or solving the derivative equation; $a=0.681137\\ldots$. The endpoints tend to zero and $A\\,\\!\\prime\\prime<0$ within this interval."
            },
            {
              "code": "A1",
              "text": "$A_{\\max}=3.601146\\ldots\\approx3.60$."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
